<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Some terminal bids weaken.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Some terminal bids weaken.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were weaker Monday at some terminals in Kansas and Oklahoma, grain merchandisers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're a little lighter on some terminal bids this morning, I guess in line with the (softness at the) Gulf last week,&quot; a south central Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, farmer selling of wheat remained slow, although one dealer in central Kansas said there had been a slight increase in selling of sorghum over the weekend.  </p>
<p>Basis values are quoted against KCBT wheat, cash dollars/bu.</p>
